+### Chat card disclosure config
+
+`ui.disclosure` controls whether transcript cards start open or collapsed, independently for five part types: `thinking`, `skillInvocation`, `toolResult` (the tool execution result body, and the standalone result card for a tool call outside the loaded history page), `toolDetails` (the tool execution details body, showing the command/file/input target), and `toolDiff` (the tool execution diff body). Each accepts one of four modes:
+
+- `none`: closed. This is the default for every part except `toolDiff`.
+- `live`: the last card of that kind in the loaded transcript, but only while the session is active.
+- `last`: the last card of that kind in the loaded transcript, independent of session activity.
+- `all`: always open. This is the default for `toolDiff`.
+
+An empty or missing `ui.disclosure` reproduces the pre-existing UI behavior exactly. The `Result` card stays open regardless of mode when the tool execution errored; it now renders alongside a diff too, where the result text used to be hidden entirely. The `Details` card is not force-opened on error, since the error text lives in `Result`. A user can still collapse any card by clicking it in any mode.
+
+```json
+{
+  "ui": {
+    "disclosure": {
+      "thinking": "all",
+      "toolDetails": "all",
+      "toolResult": "last",
+      "toolDiff": "all",
+      "eventsGroup": "last"
+    }
+  }
+}
+```
+
+A sixth subkey, `eventsGroup`, controls the summarizing events group card shown for a run of tool/event messages. It accepts one of three modes (`none` is not a valid value here, since a fully collapsed card is already the default `live` outcome once work finishes):
+
+- `live` (default): the last events group in the loaded transcript stays open while its session is active, and collapses once work finishes. This reproduces the pre-existing behavior.
+- `last`: the last events group in the loaded transcript stays open regardless of session activity.
+- `all`: every events group in the transcript stays open. On a long session history this renders substantially more DOM, since a group's body is only rendered while open.
+
+For `eventsGroup`, `last` and `live` target the last group of events in the loaded transcript, not the last entry of the transcript overall. The `live` class and `live events` label are shown only for the most recent group of an active session, independent of the chosen mode. Manual collapsing/expanding is remembered per group in any mode. Because this release also changes the storage key events groups use to persist their disclosure state, every previously saved group disclosure choice resets once after upgrading.
+
